WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.058 --> 00:00:01.690
Be free.

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:02.590
Make mistakes.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.260
Try things.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.112
This is a job about
your imagination.

00:00:08.112 --> 00:00:09.820
You're making a movie
influenced by life.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.950
You're making a character
influenced by a human,

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.420
and you want to make it
as human as possible.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.149
What is their desire?

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.900
Desire is at the
root of everything.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.320
I have not been to a
traditional drama school.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.130
I've been working for 25
years, and I learned by doing,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.110
and then I pieced
together different things

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:33.240
that are helpful for me that
I want to share with you.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.850
Green-screen acting is
kind of the purest form

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.010
of acting because
you're inventing

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.040
both what's outside of you
and what's inside of you

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.135
as an actor.

00:00:44.135 --> 00:00:46.810
We're going to do a scene
where I've just found out

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.380
my boyfriend's cheating on me,
and I'm entering his apartment.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.860
You want to scour
the space to see

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.860
what you might use that would
be emotionally relevant.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.410
Help the camera catch
what's being read.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:06.050
Get very close to the camera,
to give a feeling of what

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.220
you might be going through.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.470
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:11.330
When I was asked to
play Jackie Kennedy,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:15.380
I was terrified, which is always
a good reason to do something.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.240
I always work with
a dialect coach.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.460
 For Jackie, every
single syllable,

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.740
every breath had to
be exactly the same.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.960
 When you see where
the breaths are,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.960
you can read what is sort
of happening underneath what

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.160
the person is saying.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:31.210
This is a joyful,
creative process,

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.335
that you don't need to be
afraid of making mistakes.

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:36.770
[SNEEZES] Thank you.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.596
That's how you sneeze on cue.

00:01:38.596 --> 00:01:39.964
[LAUGHS]

00:01:39.964 --> 00:01:42.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.980
Your job is to imagine
someone else's life.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.010
That is what we do.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:49.990
We say, I wonder what that
person feels and thinks,

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.630
and that's the experience
in a movie theater.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.540
We're sharing this
social experience

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.060
with other people
for two hours, caring

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.470
about someone else's life.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.410
It's the act of empathy.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.430
I'm Natalie Portman, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.080
[MUSIC PLAYING]

